# caos-expr — ambient `/std` is GONE. Suite 29/29, `nix build` green.

Nothing is mid-edit. `design/caos-expr.md` carries the full state and the
remaining work; this file is the short version plus the lessons that do not
belong in any one file.

## Where we are

There is no `refs/caos/std`, no `/cas/std/<name>`, and no `std` arg. A workspace
declares its entry points in `./DEPS`, the root `/.caos-expr` expands them into
`DEEP-DEPS/`, and clients descend. Every `std/<name>` is a checked-in source dir
whose `.caos-expr` says how it is built; the five that cannot build themselves
(flake-builder, cargo, runner, rustc, deep-deps) name a `docker://seeded…`
sentinel and are answered by the core-seeder-runner from `refs/caos/seed`.

`build-builtins.sh` bootstraps that core and publishes nothing else. deep-deps is
one worker run. The server has no std at all.

## Remaining

1. **The consumer story** — a foreign repo needs caos in its tree: expand a
   pinned caos COMMIT into a tree inside a `.caos-expr`, then refer to
   `./flake-inputs/caos/std/foo`. Small (a commit already materializes via
   `--name:commit=`; `read_commit` gives its tree) but unbuilt, and nothing here
   needs it yet.
2. **`tests/lib/run-test.sh`'s `objects/info/alternates`** — see design doc.
   Verified still load-bearing (removing it fails 11 tests) and verified NOT
   user-facing (a fresh host client pushes fine). Why the inner client differs is
   unexplained.
3. **Comment sweep** — `caos-tools/test.sh`, `tests/lib/run-test.sh` and
   `crates/caos/src/chat.rs` still narrate history. SPEC.md: comments should
   state decisions a naive reader might undo, not the journey. build-builtins.sh
   has had this treatment; those have not.

## Lessons worth keeping

**Verify the REAL artifact.** Three wrong theories in a row came from
reconstructing a deepened tree from the HOST's std while the thing under
investigation was built from the TREE UNDER TEST's std — different builds,
different runner deltas, so the reconstruction only ever agreed with itself.
`/cas/std` seen from inside a test container was the OUTER job's, for the same
reason. `tests/deps-dump` exists for this: it asserts nothing and prints what the
harness actually delivered.

**A guard that verifies nothing is worse than no guard.** `caosd std-check`
walked std entries looking for a delta's `base`; once every entry became source
it checked ZERO digests and still said "std is intact". It now walks the seed
records and errors if it finds nothing to check.

**`nix build` with two installables and two `-o` flags does not create both
symlinks** — one is left pointing at a previous build, and the other can be
missing entirely. Build one output per invocation. (`--refresh` is NOT needed;
nix picks up dirty-tree edits fine — verified.)

**Corrections made in flight, recorded so they are not re-derived:**
- The alternates workaround is NOT a symptom of the `std` arg. Removing the arg
  did not fix it; the image closure is a separate path to the same missing
  objects.
- `worker_common::std_image` was not dead when I called it dead — the grep
  covered `crates/` and `std/` but not `tests/`.
- The empty-directory bug was real but did NOT explain the 7 rustc-tool
  failures; fixing it changed nothing there.
